333
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,440
No need to worry

334
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:47,440
Why would I worry?

335
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:50,840
Anyway

336
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,880
Would you be willing to introduce me to Captain Agu?

337
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:56,200
You're asking to meet my grandfather?

338
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:02,640
That's my full report

339
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:03,780
Hmm

340
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:09,360
So you're banking on the theory that Captain Agu and the Adola Link are connected somehow

341
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,820
That's correct, sir

342
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:13,000
I recently met a relative of his

343
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,180
Lieutenant Asako Agu of the 6th

344
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:17,080
I asked her to introduce us

345
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:17,920
Could work

346
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:22,260
I was actually just about to get in touch with the chief of the fire defense agency

347
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:26,060
I'll see if he can reach out to Company 4 on our behalf

348
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:26,920
But

349
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:31,180
If we assume the story Captain Burns told you is actually legit

350
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:36,440
Then the Whiteclad were at the very least involved in the tragedy that took your family from you

351
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:39,080
I live for the chance to get revenge on that demon

352
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:40,720
After 12 years

353
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:43,080
It hurts to think that it might have been my mother

354
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:45,100
But I was wrong about my brother's death

355
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,660
So I can't rule this out either

356
00:19:46,660 --> 00:19:48,380
Tell me this

357
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:50,980
If your mother has become an infernal

358
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:53,120
And it turns out she's still around

359
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,580
Then I'll save her

360
00:19:55,580 --> 00:19:58,340
I'll find a way to turn her back into a human being

361
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:28,320
I'll see you next time

362
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:58,320
I'll see you next time

363
00:20:58,340 --> 00:21:28,320
I'll see you next time

364
00:21:28,340 --> 00:21:36,780
What a dump

365
00:21:36,780 --> 00:21:45,460
I'm okay

366
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:46,660
I'm okay

367
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:53,800
Don't feel bad

368
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:54,960
I'm a knight

369
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:55,740
A swordsman

370
00:21:55,740 --> 00:21:56,820
So it makes sense

371
00:21:56,820 --> 00:21:58,100
I'm better at wielding a blade

372
00:21:58,100 --> 00:22:00,140
I'll pretend that this next onion's your head

373
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:02,320
I can definitely cut this faster than him

374
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:05,880
Take it easy you two

375
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:08,020
Hey what?

376
00:22:08,020 --> 00:22:09,680
Oh night king

377
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:20,220
Latom

378
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:25,560
I thoroughly enjoy it when gravel learns its place

379
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:26,940
Hello lieutenant kareem

380
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:26,960
Hello lieutenant kareem

381
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:28,900
Oh tamaki

382
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:30,280
Good to see you're here

383
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:31,620
Having a good time here

384
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:34,380
Yeah uh listen

385
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:38,100
Could you please take me off suspension

386
